  "body": "Stacked PRs:\n * #2927\n * #2926\n * #2925\n * #2924\n * #2923\n * __->__#2922\n * #2921\n * #2920\n * #2928\n\n\n--- --- ---\n\n[CuTe, SM100] Extend the S ping-pong to hd256 (1CTA and 2CTA) in the general forward\n\nhd256 fits only one Q tile per CTA in TMEM (2 x S + O = 512 columns), so on\nthe general kernel the softmax and the MMA warp serialize per KV block the\nsame way decode does: PV_i needs P_i and QK_{i+1} was issued after PV_i, so\nthe tensor pipe idles during every softmax. The S ping-pong already fixes\nthis for hd64/128 decode and nothing in it is specific to those head dims or\nto 1CTA, so allow head_dim 256, including with 2CTA instructions (the only\n2CTA config with q_stage == 1). sO overlaps sQ for hd256 (64 KB each), which\nleaves 5 KV stages with 2CTA and 2 with 1CTA; with #2817's K0, K1, V0, ...\nload order the 2-stage case is neutral to 4% faster on 1CTA decode/chunked\nshapes, so it is not excluded. hd256 with SplitKV is not supported by the\nkernel yet and stays out of the ping-pong until measured.\n\nhd256 still routes to the dedicated kernel, so no existing config changes.",
